            "description": "Publish an arbitrary MQTT message via the server's broker connection.\n\nThe example body simulates a telemetry message from an Arduino at 192.168.1.100:\n- Zone parameter ID 5: temperature = 23.5°C\n- Flowerpot parameter ID 10: soil moisture = 62%\n\nThe server will receive this via its own `greenhouse/+/status` subscription, call `updateTelemetry()`, and push the full model back to `greenhouse/192.168.1.100/set/model`.\n\nIf the greenhouse was previously `NOT_RESPONSIVE` or `OFF`, its status will change to `ON` and the model push will happen automatically.\n\n**Update the `id` values to match real IDs in your database.**"
